- **VL adjacency is Full on both sides** (control-plane appears up)

The OSPF VL re-established after r8's restart and reached Full state, but its database-exchange phase failed to deliver the single Type 4 (ASBR Summary) LSA — generated by r1 for ASBR r11 — to r8's Area 0 LSDB. Without it, r8 cannot locate the ASBR and drops all externally-redistributed routes.

=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: r8
diagnosis_text:
The OSPF virtual link (VL) between r4 (Router-ID 14.1.4.1) and r8 (Router-ID 18.1.4.1), transiting Area 1, is the mechanism joining Area 2 (r8's loopbacks and stub segment BB) to the backbone. After r8 was restarted, the VL re-formed and reached Full adjacency status — so the control plane looks healthy — but the post-restart database synchronisation over the VL silently failed to deliver one critical LSA to r8: the Type 4 ASBR Summary LSA (Link State ID 112.1.1.1, Advertising Router 111.1.1.1=r1, Metric 10) that r1 generates to advertise the location of ASBR r11 (Router-ID 112.1.1.1). Every other backbone router (r1, r3, r4, r9) carries this LSA in their Area 0 LSDB; r8's Area 0 LSDB shows exactly 72 LSAs versus the 73 everyone else holds, and its ASBR-summary section is completely empty. Without that Type 4 LSA, r8 cannot compute a path to the ASBR, so — despite possessing all 11 Type 5 AS-external LSAs (redistributed from EIGRP by r11) — it installs zero external routes. Confirmed: ping from r8 to 102.1.1.1 and 120.1.1.1 returns "Network is unreachable", while backbone router r3 reaches those same addresses with 0% loss. The OSPF intra- and inter-area routes on r8 are unaffected (r8 can reach backbone loopbacks and r11's OSPF-domain interface 111.1.1.2 normally). Root cause: after r8's restart the VL database-exchange did not propagate the pre-existing Type 4 ASBR Summary LSA from r4 to r8, leaving Area 2 blind to all AS-external destinations. Corrective fix: on r8, execute `vtysh -c "clear ip ospf process"` to tear down and rebuild the VL adjacency; the fresh Exchange/Loading cycle will re-deliver the missing Type 4 LSA, after which r8's SPF will install the external routes and connectivity will be restored.
=== END ===